    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 61 tests pass, including the new `Cp49Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the owner API to return `selfLink = '/api/owners/' + id`. The `Cp49Tests` acceptance test creates an owner, then does `GET /api/owners/{id}` and asserts `$.selfLink` equals `/api/owners/{id}` \u2014 so `selfLink` had to be a field on the returned `OwnerDto`.\n\n`OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated by MapStruct, so I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a new `selfLink` (readOnly string) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(\\\"/api/owners/\\\" + owner.getId())\")` so every owner mapped to a DTO (GET, POST, PUT responses) carries the canonical self link.\n\nThe whole suite is green (61 tests, 0 failures).",
